<title>SINGAPORE: Wing Tai lowers stake in hotel property.</title>
<headline>Wing Tai lowers stake in hotel property.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-12-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Property-based Wing Tai Holdings said on Wednesday it has lowered its effective stake in a Singapore $200 million hotel property that it plans to buy.</p>
<p>Wing Tai said its effective interest in the option to buy the Cairnhill Hotel and some adjacent houses has been changed to 50 percent from 75 percent announced earlier.</p>
<p>Rodamco N.V., a company incorporated in the Netherlands, has confirmed it will take a 25 percent interest in the property.</p>
<p>Rodamco has paid S$2 million as its proportionate contribution towards the S$8 million deposit for the option, said Wing Tai.</p>
<p>- Singapore Newsroom 65-8703080</p>
